    "created_at": "2021-03-04T19:44:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-03T09:41:53Z",
    "body": "This functionality must be optional. In forms with small size parameters it is not necessary. The browser could decide to show the progress from a certain size. Even so, I think it is better that you can choose by setting the parameter. The developer could still be interested in doing the progress dialog on their own and disable this functionality. For example for backwards compatibility with existing code. And there may be other reasons that we can't think of right now. Optional is better. \r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
